==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Ursamajor]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Capy]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone]] + [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|erasers]] works for all of these enemies. You won't be spawning much else besides Cyberpunk and the occasional attackers, so you can reach the money cap frequently throughout the battle. Bringing average ranged attackers with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] makes this stage more of a waiting game than anything else. Try to kill the pushers over less threatening enemies, like Capy, so you don't get overwhelmed, the boss waves can be used to your advantage and ensure that you don't make it to the Surge Base which can delete your stack. [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] can be good here to Slow and KB R.Ost and Master A. Ranged Ubers very well work here and they're almost needed for 3 star magnifications.

==Trivia==
*Roast Meat, Not Cities' Japanese name, Grill the Meat but Don't Burn the Town, is a reference to "grill the meat but don't burn your home," a translation of a phrase from one of Bansankan's [https://youtu.be/IUwpjwC5OjU yakiniku sauce commercials].
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,600. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

